<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Cadswep half year earnings rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Cadswep half year earnings rise.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>24 weeks ended June 14</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 17.5	  vs 14.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 3.5	   vs 2.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts are expecting interim earnings per share on a range of 17.2 cents to 17.6 and a dividend of 3.4 cents 3.5. The consensus figures were for earnings of 17.4 cents and a dividend of 3.44. In June the firm had a ten for one share split which dilutes profits per share by ten times.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   64.85	 vs 53.73</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   59.59	 vs 51.09</p>
<p>    Tax			 15.49	 vs 13.39</p>
<p>    Financing costs	 2.23	  vs 2.63</p>
<p>    Turnover		  639.89	vs 544.45</p>
<p>Div payable October 3</p>
<p>on register September 12</p>
<p>Full name: Cadbury Schweppes South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said in a statement with its results that the outlook for general consumer demand continued to be weak, but it was confident it could deliver real earnings growth as long as current demand in its own markets was sustained.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
